// ForkSession clones a session into a new, fully independent session (no data
// is shared with or read through to the source). The clone is inclusive of
// up_to_message_id and extends to just before the next user/assistant message,
// so an assistant message's tool results always come with it. Empty
// up_to_message_id clones the whole history.
//
// Copied: session settings (provider/model, tools, prompt sections, tool policy,
// compression, tags, surface, title) and the history plus its per-turn data
// (turn metadata, tool-result sidecars, decorations, tracked-document versions).
// Not copied: provider-side session state — the fork's first turn replays its
// history as a fresh provider session, exactly like a provider/model switch —
// nor the event log, cache, draft or queue.
//
// Errors: NOT_FOUND (unknown source or message), ALREADY_EXISTS (new_session_id
